{"created": "2026-11-06T00:15:27.462757+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-06T00:15:27.753150+00:00", "id": 23991050, "conceptrecid": "22862110", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23991050", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22862110", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23991050", "metadata": {"title": "Data and verification scripts for \"A Half-Shift Criterion on Three-Colour 12\u00d712 Grids\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23991050", "publication_date": "2026-11-05", "description": "<p class=\"FirstParagraph\">Companion article &ldquo;From Ansate Cross Colourings to Unified Patterns and Sound Forms&rdquo;, version 2.20, in English and French, together with its supplement C1&ndash;C6, certificates and independent audit. The data and scripts of the half-shift criterion on three-colour 12 &times; 12 grids are kept unchanged in half-shift-cube-v3/. Versions 2.18 and 2.19 of the article are kept.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\">Version 2.20 extends Section 24: - the XOR-translation stabiliser of the directional corpus of 379,920 patterns at order 30 is trivial in the 55-bit option encoding; replacement graphs, a six-group threshold, a conditional four-bit action on 336 words and a partial covering by sixteen-word families (258,192 of 379,920 words); the structural origin of the factor sixteen remains open; - whole-diamond balance at source orders 18, 30 and 42, and the partition of the order-18 balanced corpus into 858 families of 256 patterns; - a listening experiment on a family of 256 at order 18, a computed sonification and not a physical measurement.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\">New proof folders (preuves/) hold the scripts, data and reports for the eighth setting across the 858 families, the exact invariance of one spectral shell in 32 families at order 18, its compensated analogue at order 30 and a transfer to order 42. The statistics over the 858 families describe the chosen pairing of positions.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\">The finite counts are counts within the stated domains (second cross, J covering, group I, three-cell-block code). They do not classify all patterns or all magic squares.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\">Licences: code under AGPL v3, with a commercial licence on request; article texts under CC BY 4.0; data and generated files under CC BY-NC 4.0.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Amiot, Anibal Edelberto", "affiliation": "ORCID", "orcid": "0009-0002-6414-9448"}], "keywords": ["magic squares", "half-shift criterion", "three-colour grids", "Jacquard weaving", "cube edge rule", "exhaustive enumeration", "verification", "combinatorics", "recreational mathematics", "spectral invariance", "certificates", "isospectral patterns", "iscrete cosine transform"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22722485", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-book", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22945021", "relation": "isReferencedBy", "resource_type": "publication-report", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22966839", "relation": "isReferencedBy", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/anibaledel/livreedhermes", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22866061", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22866061", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22986529", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "2.20", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/anibaledel/livreedhermes"}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "apgl-v3"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 4, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22862110"}}]}}, "title": "Dat